From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guacamole_nura rc4 proposal <nura-rc4@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: guacamole: add gated goodix fingerprint node

Add the Goodix under-display fingerprint node and its IRQ pinctrl state
for the OnePlus 7 Pro. The node keeps the stock pin assignment (GPIO 101
supply, 118 interrupt, 131 reset) and the downstream chip/lcd names read
by /proc/fp_id and /proc/lcd_type.

The node is deliberately status = "disabled": rc4 ships gate-1
groundwork, not authentication. Leave it disabled until gate 0
(QCOMTEE/QTEE) is verified on the phone, then change it to "okay" and
load goodix_fp with allow_power=1 for the gate-1 reset test.

GPIO 90 is the stock sensor-variant ID strap. This driver does not read
it; the chip name comes from the node. GPIOs 90, 101, 118 and 131 are
unused in the 7.0 guacamole tree; 90 and 101 only appear in default
pinctrl states of unused QUP SPI groups.

Signed-off-by: guacamole_nura rc4 proposal <nura-rc4@example.invalid>
Nura-Category: device-dt
Nura-Origin: nura rc4 fingerprint topic
Upstream-Status: n/a: guacamole DTS is not upstream
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole.dts
@@ -133,4 +133,6 @@
 
 #include "sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi"
 
+#include "sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-fingerprint.dtsi"
+
 #include "sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-rear.dtsi"
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-fingerprint.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * OnePlus 7 Pro (guacamole) Goodix optical fingerprint sensor, for kernel
+ * patch 0051 (goodix_fp).
+ *
+ * Pins and names from the stock device tree, LineageOS
+ * android_kernel_oneplus_sm8150 (lineage-23.2),
+ * arch/arm64/boot/dts/18821/sm8150-mtp.dtsi (oplus_fp_common, goodix_fp) and
+ * sm8150-pinctrl.dtsi (gpio_goodix_irq_default):
+ *   GPIO 90  sensor variant ID, pull-up input (not consumed by 0051)
+ *   GPIO 101 supply enable, high = on (power-mode 2)
+ *   GPIO 118 interrupt, rising edge, 2 mA, no bias
+ *   GPIO 131 reset, low = held in reset
+ *
+ * The include is placed after the nura delta and before the rear-camera
+ * include, so the end-of-file slot stays free for the popup-camera include.
+ *
+ * GATE 1 IS DISABLED ON PURPOSE. Leave status = "disabled" until gate 0
+ * (QCOMTEE/QTEE) has been verified on the phone. To run the gate-1 test,
+ * change status to "okay" AND load goodix_fp with allow_power=1. Both steps
+ * are required; either one alone cannot power or reset the sensor.
+ */
+/ {
+	fingerprint {
+		compatible = "goodix,goodix_fp";
+		status = "disabled";
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 118 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 131 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		power-gpios = <&tlmm 101 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		pinctrl-0 = <&fp_irq_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		/* /proc/fp_id and /proc/lcd_type, read by the stock HAL */
+		oplus,chip-name = "G_OPTICAL_18821_G2_4";
+		oplus,lcd-type = "samsung";
+	};
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	fp_irq_default: fp-irq-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio118";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-disable;
+		input-enable;
+	};
+};
